t 8-3 to the only team it couldn't beat.", "At the other end of Main Street, Zero Fox Given beat nobody. Not one team in all-play, a 9-2 loss to Acinonyx, and not a single roster move all week. Luka Dončić hung 52 on them Sunday just to make sure the body stayed down.", "Defending champ Thug Life opened the title defense with a 6-5 loss to LeParth James, who won the week with three players on the floor Sunday. Mikal Bridges went 0 for 10 from three. The belt is already loose."], "sections": {"results": "Showdown at High Noon", "results_sub": "Every gunfight from Week 1, with the score after each day. Read left to right to see who blinked.", "late": "Dead Man's Hand", "late_sub": "What changed over the last two days. Saturday and Sunday decide more weeks than Tuesday ever will.", "wanted": "Wanted", "wanted_sub": "Posted by order of the commissioner's office.", "guns": "Fastest Guns in the West", "guns_sub": "The five best lines of the week, by value across all 11 categories.", "fools": "Fool's Gold", "fools_sub": "Auction picks that cost $20 or more and shot blanks.", "boot": "Boot Hill", "boot_sub": "Who got carried off the field. Priciest bodies first.", "roy": "Rest of Year: The Long Ride", "roy_sub": "Updated team projections after Sunday's card. Ranked on Yahoo's rest-of-season projections, pulled Monday morning, with Victory Road's playoff odds beside them.", "saloon": "Saloon Talk", "saloon_sub": "One round for every manager. Nobody drinks free."}, "wanted": {"mvp": {"title": "Sheriff", "line": "Swept the all-play 11-0. Owns the town until further notice."}, "dud": {"title": "Wanted: Dead Weight", "line": "Beat zero of 11 teams. Last seen not making roster moves."}, "luckiest": {"title": "Horse Thief", "line": "Went 9-2 with a roster that plays like a .612 team. Somebody check the saddlebags."}, "robbed": {"title": "Bushwhacked", "line": "Beat 7 of 11 teams and still lost 8-3, because the schedule sent the Sheriff."}}, "late": {"web.l.39751.t.5|web.l.39751.t.8": "Suggs to be you led 6-5 through Friday. MONSTARS ☄️ flipped it to 7-4 on Saturday behind Jalen Johnson and Ty Jerome, who went 14 for 14 at the line over the weekend. Then Sunday came: Scottie Barnes went 0 for 12, the lead bled out, and Chris settled for a 5-5-1 tie with Cooper Flagg sitting in his opponent's IL slot.", "web.l.39751.t.7|web.l.39751.t.10": "Nova Knicks led 9-2 through Friday and coasted. White Mambas got 42 points and 8 threes from Jamal Murray over the weekend and stole back DREB and AST. Too little, too late, and Vishal still made zero moves to help it.", "web.l.39751.t.1|web.l.39751.t.12": "theInfamous was down 9-2 Friday and clawed back one category. Anthony Black hit 5 of 7 from three over the weekend. It was still an 8-3 burial.", "web.l.39751.t.2|web.l.39751.t.11": "Acinonyx was already up 8-2-1. Luka's 52 on Sunday just added BLK to the pile."}, "boot": "Cooper Flagg ($43) played twice and went to the IL. Stephen Curry ($31) sat on John J's bench Saturday and is on IL now. Kon Knueppel ($21) never left Thug Life's IL slot all week. Jalen Duren, Paolo Banchero and Joel Embiid all landed there Sunday.", "roy": "The board doesn't care about Week 1. White Mambas went 4-7 and Yahoo's projections rank the roster first the rest of the way. Gopher Gold swept the all-play, owns a near lock on the playoffs, and projects ninth. Zero Fox Given projects last, which tracks.", "zingers": {"web.l.39751.t.1": "John J made 7 moves and still got shot 8-3. Darius Acuff Jr. went 24 for 73. That's not a rookie, that's a firing squad.", "web.l.39751.t.2": "Eshan went 9-2 on a roster the all-play math calls a .612 team. Luka dropped 52 Sunday. Nikola Vučević started once and scored 0. Enjoy the stolen horse.", "web.l.39751.t.3": "Adarsh beat 7 of 11 teams and lost 8-3 because he drew the Sheriff. AJ Dybantsa and Jimmy Butler III spent the whole week in the IL slot collecting dust.", "web.l.39751.t.4": "Phil swept the all-play 11-0 and Sabonis shot 21 for 26. Hold the parade: Yahoo's rest-of-season projections rank this roster ninth.", "web.l.39751.t.5": "Chris trailed 6-5 Friday, led 7-4 Saturday, and tied 5-5-1 Sunday. Two moves all week. Jalen Green went 9 for 22 and Jalen Duren is on IL.", "web.l.39751.t.6": "Parth beat the defending champ 6-5 with three players on the floor Sunday. De'Anthony Melton started and scored 0. Joel Embiid is back in the IL slot, right where he left it.", "web.l.39751.t.7": "Roshan won 7-4, then added Noah Clowney, Scotty Pippen Jr. and De'Andre Hunter inside three minutes Sunday night. That's not a waiver strategy, that's a bar fight.", "web.l.39751.t.8": "Keshav paid $43 for Cooper Flagg. Flagg played twice and hit the IL. Keshav still clawed back from 7-4 down Saturday to a tie, which is the most work anyone on this team did.", "web.l.39751.t.9": "The defending champ opened with a 6-5 loss. Mikal Bridges went 5 for 23 and 0 for 10 from three. Kon Knueppel ($21) never left the IL slot. The belt is on loan.", "web.l.39751.t.10": "Vishal made zero moves and lost 7-4. Josh Giddey ($35) shot 7 for 26. The scary part: Yahoo projects this roster first the rest of the way, so he'll call it a plan.", "web.l.39751.t.11": "Sagar beat zero of 11 teams, lost 9-2 and made zero moves. The only thing moving in that saloon is the tumbleweed.", "web.l.39751.t.12": "Jason won 8-3 and Shai went 32 for 72. The luck meter says this is a .599 team wearing a .727 hat. Enjoy it while the hat fits."}, "sign_off": "Next week the Gazette goes undercover. Spy Edition, Monday morning."}}